ntent-backed variant? No, with `content=` it stores the doc text internal AND still consults content table.\n\nActually, maybe the corruption came from the malformed `INSERT OR REPLACE ... VALUES('rebuild')` in the previous run? Better-sqlite3 might have left a corrupted in-memory database state from that. But tests create fresh in-memory DBs each `beforeEach`. Hmm.\n\nWait, I see something: in notes.test.ts, line 167:\n`appCtx.db.prepare(\"INSERT INTO notes (title, body, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('Old', 'Body', '2020-01-01 00:00:00', '2020-01-01 00:00:00')\").run();`\n\nThis direct insert should fire triggers and populate FTS. Then the PUT updates it. But the test failed at the same spot before and after my fix. \n\nActually, wait. The 404s on search — maybe the search routes aren't registered because server.ts is cached by tsx, or because there's some import issue. But the existing CRUD tests pass (except corruption), so routes.ts IS loaded.\n\nLet me check if the search route path maybe conflicts. In Express, `/notes/:id` and `/notes/search` — order matters. I added search AFTER `/notes/:id`, so a request to `/notes/search` would match `/notes/:id` with `id='search'`! That's why I get 404 — it tries to get a note with id=search. And `/notes/search/suggest` matches `/notes/:id` with id='search/suggest'! \n\nBut wait, Express matches routes in order. `/notes/search` should be defined before `/notes/:id`. I added them after /notes/:id. That's the cause of the 404s. And for suggest, since it's interpreted as `/notes/:id` where id = \"search/suggest\", then it calls get note, doesn't find it, throws NotFoundError, and returns 404.\n\nFor the corruption issue, after moving search routes before /notes/:id, tests will exercise FTS more, but the corruption in PUT test might still exist.\n\nLet me reorder the routes: search routes should come before `/notes/:id`.\n\nActually, I should put `/notes/search/suggest` AND `/notes/search` before `/notes/:id`. The order shou